# Cyber Sooho — Visual Constitution (always)

Full text: [`project/CONSTITUTION.md`](project/CONSTITUTION.md). If UI work conflicts with that file, **follow the constitution**, not modern redesign instincts.

## Dual-stack

- **Under the hood**: modern stack OK (React, Vite, TS, Tailwind, Supabase, Vercel).
- **On screen**: Web 1.0 full replica; **Windows Classic (95/98/2000)** is the visual law.

## Must look like

- Desktop teal / classic wallpaper + **single ~800px app window**
- Chrome: title bar, menu bar, tabs, status bar
- 3D bevels: light from **top-left**
  - Raised/outset buttons: light top-left, dark bottom-right
  - Sunken/inset inputs/content: reverse
- Face `#c0c0c0`, highlight `#fff`/`#dfdfdf`, shadow `#808080`/`#404040`, title `#000080`→`#1084d0`, select `#000080`, desktop `#008080`

## Typography & media

- Prefer pixel/dot fonts already in project (`ThinRounded`, `DungGeunMo`, Tahoma for chrome). No Inter/Roboto/system-ui SaaS look.
- Keep `image-rendering: pixelated` and custom cursors.
- Motion: click/press only. No soft fades, springs, parallax, glass, neon glow.

## Forbidden UI

- Rounded marketing cards, pill CTAs, soft multi-layer shadows, glassmorphism, purple gradients, hero landing layouts, flat Material/iOS chrome that removes bevels.
- Native `input[type=range]` blue round thumbs; native `input[type=color]` OS pickers — use `ClassicSlider` + `ColorPickerDialog` instead.

## Implementation

- Reuse `WindowFrame`, `WindowsTitleBar`, `MenuBar`, `Navigation` — do not invent a new shell.
- Tailwind is a tool; output must still be Classic. Avoid `rounded-xl`, `shadow-lg`, `backdrop-blur` as defaults.
- Before shipping UI changes, re-read `project/CONSTITUTION.md` Do/Don’t checklist.

## Performance defaults (CONSTITUTION §5)

For board/tab/list UIs, always apply:
- SWR-style table cache (`boardQueryCache`) — paint cache, quiet revalidate, invalidate on mutate
- Slim `listSelect` (no gallery/base64/`select('*')` on lists); hydrate full row on detail/edit
- Visit-once keep-alive (`KeepAlivePanels`) + shared content `min-height` — no window jump on section switch

## Bilingual defaults (CONSTITUTION §6)

Site is **ko + en** (MenuBar flag toggle). For every new feature / UI string:
- No hardcoded Korean/English UI copy — use `useLocale().t('key')` + `src/i18n/messages.ts`
- Add **both** `ko` and `en` keys in the same change; never “English later”
- Alerts/confirms/prompts and thrown user-facing errors must go through `t()` / i18n keys
- Do **not** auto-translate user content (posts, guestbook, marquee DB text)
- Check EN layout length so Classic chrome does not break
